WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.196
everyone, welcome to Community & Code.

00:00:02.436 --> 00:00:04.564
I'm your host, Chris Reynolds.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.745
So quick question,

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.667
what's scarier than speaking in front of

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.648
your three hundred plus person company?

00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:13.442
speaking in front of eleven hundred

00:00:13.482 --> 00:00:14.723
strangers at DevRelCon.

00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:16.925
But that is what my guest this week

00:00:16.965 --> 00:00:18.787
did to get over her fear of speaking

00:00:18.827 --> 00:00:19.247
in public.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.489
And it maybe worked out a little too

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:21.789
well.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.772
Jacquie Capur started out as a music

00:00:24.812 --> 00:00:25.152
major,

00:00:25.332 --> 00:00:27.174
but was already building Neopets and

00:00:27.214 --> 00:00:29.276
MySpace profile pages on the side before

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:30.797
deciding that these computer things she

00:00:30.837 --> 00:00:32.859
did was actually something that she could

00:00:32.919 --> 00:00:33.980
do as a full-time gig.

00:00:35.012 --> 00:00:37.313
She landed in DevOps and eventually found

00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:39.854
her way into DevRel at AWS, HashiCorp,

00:00:39.954 --> 00:00:40.835
and now Nebius.

00:00:40.895 --> 00:00:41.615
And along the way,

00:00:42.115 --> 00:00:44.356
she ended up on a live coding reality

00:00:44.396 --> 00:00:47.257
TV show that was basically the great big

00:00:47.358 --> 00:00:50.479
British bake-off with a compiler.


00:43:08.011 --> 00:43:08.875
I'd love to hear your thoughts and

00:43:08.895 --> 00:43:09.335
insights.

00:43:09.817 --> 00:43:10.861
Yeah, thanks.

00:43:10.881 --> 00:43:11.683
Thank you.
